.TH "WEBTRANSPORTSENDSTREAM.GETWRITER" "3JS" "April 13, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
WebTransportSendStream.getWriter \- WebTransportSendStream: getWriter()
method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]getWriter()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]WebTransportSendStream\f[R] interface returns a new
\f[CR]WebTransportWriter\f[R] object and locks the stream to that
instance.
While the stream is locked, no other writer can be acquired until this
one is released.
.PP
\f[CR]WebTransportWriter\f[R] is a subclass of
\f[CR]WritableStreamDefaultWriter\f[R] that additionally provides the
\f[CR]atomicWrite()\f[R] and \f[CR]commit()\f[R] methods.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
getWriter()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]WebTransportWriter\f[R] object instance.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
The stream is already locked to another writer.
.SH EXAMPLES
The following example shows how to open a unidirectional stream over a
\f[CR]WebTransport\f[R] connection and use \f[CR]getWriter()\f[R] to
write chunks of data to it.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] transport = \f[B]new\f[R] WebTransport(\(dqhttps://example.com/webtransport\(dq);
\f[B]await\f[R] transport.ready;

\f[B]const\f[R] stream = \f[B]await\f[R] transport.createUnidirectionalStream();
\f[B]const\f[R] writer = stream.getWriter();

\f[B]const\f[R] encoder = \f[B]new\f[R] TextEncoder();
\f[B]await\f[R] writer.write(encoder.encode(\(dqHello\(dq));
\f[B]await\f[R] writer.write(encoder.encode(\(dq, world!\(dq));
\f[B]await\f[R] writer.close();
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
